// A slice on an Instance that does not define __slice__ stays a fatal slice
// error. Native raises it through Op::SLICE's RAISE_ERROR site; the JVM
// backend must raise a raw LoxError, not a catchable Error value. The live
// catch below must not stop it, so both sides print nothing and exit non-zero.
class V {}
try { V()[0:1]; } catch (e) { print "caught"; }
